  "title": "Normal Pediatric Vital Signs",
  "markdown": "# Normal Pediatric Vital Signs\n\n![Visual reference from Normal Pediatric Vital Signs](../../assets/figures/page-0140-visual.webp)\n\n| Age | Approximate Weight (kg) | Pulse/Min | Resp/Min | Minimum Systolic BP | Glucose (mg/dl) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Newborn | 3 | 100-160 | 30-60 | 60 | 45-120 |\n| 6 months | 7 | 100-160 | 30-60 | 70 | 100-180 |\n| 1 year | 10 | 100-140 | 24-40 | 70 | 100-180 |\n| 2 years | 12 | 80-130 | 24-40 | 70 | 100-180 |\n| 3 | 15 | 80-130 | 24-40 | Multiply age x 2 and add 70 | 100-180 |\n| 4 | 16 | 80-120 | 22-34 | Multiply age x 2 and add 70 | 100-180 |\n| 5 | 18 | 80-120 | 22-34 | Multiply age x 2 and add 70 | 100-180 |\n| 6-7 | 20 | 70-110 | 18-30 | Multiply age x 2 and add 70 | 80-140 |\n| 8-9 | 25 | 70-110 | 18-30 | Multiply age x 2 and add 70 | 80-140 |\n| 10-11 | 35 | 60-100 | 16-24 | Multiply age x 2 and add 70 | 70-120 |\n| 12-13 | 40 | 60-100 | 16-24 | Multiply age x 2 and add 70 | 70-120 |\n| 14 | 50 | 60-100 | 16-24 | Multiply age x 2 and add 70 | 70-120 |\n| 15 | 55+ | 60-100 | 14-20 | Multiply age x 2 and add 70 | 70-120 |\n\n> Note: Estimated weight in kilograms: [2 x (age in years)] + 8\n> \\* Typical Systolic BP in children 1-10 years of age: 90 + (age in years x 2)\n> \\* Lower Limits of Systolic BP for a child age 3-15 years: 70 + (age in years x 2)\n",
  "plain_text": "Normal Pediatric Vital Signs Age Approximate Weight (kg) Pulse/Min Resp/Min Minimum Systolic BP Glucose (mg/dl) Newborn 3 100-160 30-60 60 45-120 6 months 7 100-160 30-60 70 100-180 1 year 10 100-140 24-40 70 100-180 2 years 12 80-130 24-40 70 100-180 3 15 80-130 24-40 Multiply age x 2 and add 70 100-180 4 16 80-120 22-34 Multiply age x 2 and add 70 100-180 5 18 80-120 22-34 Multiply age x 2 and add 70 100-180 6-7 20 70-110 18-30 Multiply age x 2 and add 70 80-140 8-9 25 70-110 18-30 Multiply age x 2 and add 70 80-140 10-11 35 60-100 16-24 Multiply age x 2 and add 70 70-120 12-13 40 60-100 16-24 Multiply age x 2 and add 70 70-120 14 50 60-100 16-24 Multiply age x 2 and add 70 70-120 15 55+ 60-100 14-20 Multiply age x 2 and add 70 70-120 Note: Estimated weight in kilograms: [2 x (age in years)] + 8 Typical Systolic BP in children 1-10 years of age: 90 + (age in years x 2) Lower Limits of Systolic BP for a child age 3-15 years: 70 + (age in years x 2)",
